// Authored A2 curriculum, Unit 7: health, feelings and advice.
Map<String, dynamic> _u7(int n, String title, String explanation, String example, String french, String question, List<String> options, int answer, String correction) => <String, dynamic>{'id':'A2-U07-L${n.toString().padLeft(2,'0')}',’level':'A2',’title':title,’subtitle':'Santé, émotions et conseils • Leçon $n/50',’explanation':explanation,’example':example,’french':french,’question':question,’options':options,’answer':answer,’correction':correction,’unit':7,’phase':0};
final List<Map<String,dynamic>> a2Unit7CourseData = <Map<String,dynamic>>[
_u7(1,'Common health problems','Use have a headache, a cough or a cold to describe common problems.','I have a headache today.','J’ai mal à la tête aujourd’hui.','Which phrase describes head pain?',['a headache',’a stomach',’a tooth'],0,'A headache is pain in your head.'),
_u7(2,'A sore throat','Use have a sore throat when your throat hurts.','She has a sore throat and cannot sing.','Elle a mal à la gorge et ne peut pas chanter.','Complete: I have ___ sore throat.',['a',’an',’the'],0,'Sore begins with a consonant sound, so use a.'),
_u7(3,'A stomach ache','Stomach ache names pain in the stomach; stomachache is also one word.','He stayed home because he had a stomach ache.','Il est resté à la maison parce qu’il avait mal au ventre.','What does stomach ache mean?',['back pain',’stomach pain',’ear pain'],1,'A stomach ache is pain in the stomach.'),
_u7(4,'A toothache','Use toothache for pain in a tooth or teeth.','I cannot eat because I have toothache.','Je ne peux pas manger parce que j’ai mal aux dents.','Choose the correct word for tooth pain.',['toothache',’toothhurt',’teethpain'],0,'Toothache is the standard noun.'),
_u7(5,'A cough','Use have a cough to describe repeated coughing.','My little brother has a bad cough.','Mon petit frère a une forte toux.','Complete: She has ___ cough.',['a',’an',’some'],0,'Cough is a singular countable noun here.'),
_u7(6,'A cold','Have a cold means to suffer from a common cold.','I think I am getting a cold.','Je crois que je prends un rhume.','Which expression means avoir un rhume?',['make a cold',’have a cold',’do a cold'],1,'The natural expression is have a cold.'),
_u7(7,'A fever','Use have a fever when body temperature is unusually high.','The child has a fever.','L’enfant a de la fièvre.','A fever is…',['a high body temperature',’a broken arm',’a sore foot'],0,'Fever means an unusually high body temperature.'),
_u7(8,'Feel ill','Use feel ill to describe being unwell.','I feel ill, so I am going to rest.','Je me sens malade, alors je vais me reposer.','Choose the correct form.',['I feels ill.','I feel ill.','I feeling ill.'],1,'Use the base verb feel with I.'),
_u7(9,'Feel better','Use feel better when someone’s condition improves.','You will feel better after some rest.','Tu te sentiras mieux après un peu de repos.','Feel better means…',['become healthier',’become angrier',’get lost'],0,'Feel better describes improvement.'),
_u7(10,'Feel worse','Use feel worse when a condition becomes less good.','If you feel worse, call the clinic.','Si tu te sens plus mal, appelle la clinique.','Worse is the opposite of…',['better',’sicker',’tired'],0,'Better and worse are opposites.'),
_u7(11,'At the pharmacy','Ask for medicine politely with Could I have…?','Could I have something for a cough, please?','Pourrais-je avoir quelque chose contre la toux, s’il vous plaît ?','Which request is polite?',['Give cough medicine!','Could I have something for a cough?','I take cough now.'],1,'Could I have…? is a polite request.'),
_u7(12,'Medicine instructions','Follow dosage instructions exactly; take is commonly used with medicine.','Take this medicine after meals.','Prenez ce médicament après les repas.','Complete: ___ this medicine twice a day.',['Take','Taking','Takes'],0,'Use the base verb for an instruction.'),
_u7(13,'At the doctor','Use I have an appointment to explain a planned visit.','I have an appointment with the doctor at ten.','J’ai rendez-vous chez le médecin à dix heures.','Which phrase means avoir un rendez-vous?',['make appointment',’have an appointment',’do an appointment'],1,'Have an appointment is the usual phrase.'),
_u7(14,'Describing symptoms','Use I have been feeling… for a condition continuing until now.','I have been feeling dizzy since this morning.','J’ai des vertiges depuis ce matin.','Which word means dizzy?',['having the feeling that things spin',’very hungry',’very cold'],0,'Dizzy describes a spinning or unsteady feeling.'),
_u7(15,'Since and for with symptoms','Use since with a starting point and for with a duration.','I have had this cough for three days.','J’ai cette toux depuis trois jours.','Choose the correct phrase.',['since three days',’for three days',’during three days'],1,'For introduces a length of time.'),
_u7(16,'Giving simple advice with should','Use should + base verb to give advice.','You should drink more water.','Tu devrais boire plus d’eau.','Complete: You ___ see a doctor.',['should',’should to',’shoulds'],0,'Should is followed by the base verb without to.'),
_u7(17,'Negative advice with should not','Use should not or shouldn’t to advise against an action.','You should not take more than the recommended dose.','Tu ne devrais pas dépasser la dose recommandée.','Which means tu ne devrais pas?',['should',’shouldn’t',’must'],1,'Shouldn’t is the contraction of should not.'),
_u7(18,'Advice with ought to','Ought to has a meaning similar to should.','You ought to get some rest.','Tu devrais te reposer un peu.','Complete: You ought ___ rest.',['to',’for',’at'],0,'The expression is ought to + base verb.'),
_u7(19,'Must for strong necessity','Use must when something is important or necessary.','You must wear a seat belt.','Tu dois porter une ceinture de sécurité.','Must expresses…',['strong necessity',’past ability',’a past habit'],0,'Must expresses obligation or strong necessity.'),
_u7(20,'Must not for prohibition','Must not means that an action is not allowed.','You must not smoke in the hospital.','Il est interdit de fumer à l’hôpital.','Must not means…',['it is optional',’it is forbidden',’it is a good idea'],1,'Must not expresses prohibition.'),
_u7(21,'Have to for obligation','Use have to for rules or obligations.','I have to take my sister to the clinic.','Je dois accompagner ma sœur à la clinique.','Complete: He ___ to rest.',['have',’has',’having'],1,'He takes has to.'),
_u7(22,'Don’t have to','Don’t have to means something is not necessary, not forbidden.','You don’t have to come early.','Tu n’es pas obligé de venir tôt.','Don’t have to means…',['it is forbidden',’it is not necessary',’you must do it'],1,'It expresses absence of necessity.'),
_u7(23,'Should versus must','Should gives advice; must expresses stronger obligation.','You should exercise, but you must follow safety rules.','Tu devrais faire de l’exercice, mais tu dois respecter les règles de sécurité.','Which is generally stronger?',['should',’must',’could'],1,'Must is stronger than should.'),
_u7(24,'Rest and recovery','Use get some rest to recommend relaxing or sleeping.','You look tired; get some rest.','Tu as l’air fatigué ; repose-toi un peu.','Which phrase means repose-toi?',['get some rest',’make a rest',’do resting'],0,'Get some rest is a natural expression.'),
_u7(25,'Healthy food','Use healthy to describe food that supports good health.','Fresh vegetables are part of a healthy diet.','Les légumes frais font partie d’une alimentation saine.','Healthy means…',['good for your health',’very expensive',’difficult to find'],0,'Healthy means beneficial to health.'),
_u7(26,'Exercise regularly','Use regularly to describe an action done often.','She exercises regularly after school.','Elle fait régulièrement de l’exercice après l’école.','Regularly means…',['once by chance',’often, as a habit',’never'],1,'Regularly means repeatedly at intervals.'),
_u7(27,'Sleep enough','Use enough after a verb or before a noun to express a sufficient amount.','Teenagers need to sleep enough.','Les adolescents doivent dormir suffisamment.','Which word means suffisamment?',['enough',’almost',’quite'],0,'Enough means as much as needed.'),
_u7(28,'Keep fit','Keep fit means maintain physical fitness.','Walking every day helps me keep fit.','Marcher chaque jour m’aide à garder la forme.','Keep fit means…',['stay physically healthy',’stop moving',’eat quickly'],0,'Keep fit means maintain good physical condition.'),
_u7(29,'Emotions: happy and sad','Use feel + adjective to describe an emotion.','He feels happy about his exam result.','Il est heureux de son résultat d’examen.','Choose the correct sentence.',['He feel happy.','He feels happy.','He feeling happy.'],1,'Use feels with he in the present simple.'),
_u7(30,'Angry with someone','Use angry with a person and angry about a situation.','She is angry with her brother.','Elle est fâchée contre son frère.','Which preposition fits a person?',['with',’at to',’from'],0,'Angry with someone is a common pattern.'),
_u7(31,'Worried about','Use worried about before the subject causing concern.','I am worried about tomorrow’s test.','Je suis inquiet pour le contrôle de demain.','Complete: worried ___ the exam.',['about',’for to',’at'],0,'Worried about introduces the concern.'),
_u7(32,'Excited about','Use excited about to express enthusiastic anticipation.','They are excited about the school trip.','Ils sont enthousiastes à propos de la sortie scolaire.','Excited describes…',['strong positive anticipation',’deep sleep',’physical pain'],0,'Excited means very enthusiastic.'),
_u7(33,'Bored with','Use bored with when something is no longer interesting.','I am bored with this television programme.','Je m’ennuie de cette émission télévisée.','Which phrase is correct?',['bored with',’bored from',’bored at to'],0,'Bored with is the usual pattern.'),
_u7(34,'Feel nervous','Nervous describes worry before an event or challenge.','I feel nervous before speaking English.','Je suis nerveux avant de parler anglais.','Nervous is closest to…',['worried or anxious',’very sleepy',’very thirsty'],0,'Nervous describes anxiety or worry.'),
_u7(35,'Calm down','Calm down means become less upset or anxious.','Take a deep breath and calm down.','Respire profondément et calme-toi.','Calm down means…',['become calmer',’become louder',’run away'],0,'Calm down means relax or become less upset.'),
_u7(36,'Apologising for a problem','Use I’m sorry to apologise.','I’m sorry I am late.','Je suis désolé d’être en retard.','Which is an apology?',['I’m sorry.','I’m certain.','I’m ready.'],0,'I’m sorry is a common apology.'),
_u7(37,'Responding to an apology','Use That’s all right or No problem to accept an apology.','“I’m sorry.” “That’s all right.”','« Je suis désolé. » « Ce n’est pas grave. »','Which response accepts an apology?',['That’s all right.','Never mind me not.','I sorry too.'],0,'That’s all right can reassure someone.'),
_u7(38,'Asking how someone feels','Use How do you feel? to ask about a person’s condition.','How do you feel this morning?','Comment te sens-tu ce matin ?','Choose the correct question.',['How you feel?','How do you feel?','How are feel you?'],1,'Present-simple questions use do + subject + verb.'),
_u7(39,'Asking what is wrong','What’s wrong? asks about a problem.','You look upset. What’s wrong?','Tu as l’air contrarié. Qu’est-ce qui ne va pas ?','What’s wrong? asks…',['about a problem',’for a person’s address',’about the time'],0,'It is a natural question about a difficulty.'),
_u7(40,'Explaining a reason with because','Use because to introduce the reason for something.','I stayed home because I felt ill.','Je suis resté à la maison parce que je me sentais malade.','Because introduces…',['a reason',’a comparison',’a question tag'],0,'Because links an action to its reason.'),
_u7(41,'Result with so','Use so to introduce a result.','I had a fever, so I went to the clinic.','J’avais de la fièvre, alors je suis allé à la clinique.','So introduces…',['a result',’a condition',’a possession'],0,'So connects a cause to its result.'),
_u7(42,'When to use a clinic','Use clinic for a place where people receive medical care.','The nurse works at the local clinic.','L’infirmière travaille à la clinique locale.','A clinic is a place for…',['medical care',’buying clothes',’watching films'],0,'A clinic provides healthcare services.'),
_u7(43,'Emergency language','Use Call an ambulance in an urgent medical emergency.','Please call an ambulance; he cannot breathe.','Appelez une ambulance, s’il vous plaît ; il ne peut pas respirer.','What should you call in a serious emergency?',['an ambulance',’a taxi only',’a delivery van'],0,'An ambulance transports people needing urgent medical care.'),
_u7(44,'Body parts: back','Use back to name the rear part of the body.','My back hurts after carrying the box.','J’ai mal au dos après avoir porté la boîte.','Which body part is le dos?',['back',’knee',’neck'],0,'Back means le dos.'),
_u7(45,'Body parts: shoulder','Shoulder names the joint between the arm and the body.','He hurt his shoulder while playing football.','Il s’est blessé à l’épaule en jouant au football.','Shoulder means…',['épaule',’cheville',’poignet'],0,'Shoulder is the English word for épaule.'),
_u7(46,'Body parts: knee','Knee names the joint in the middle of the leg.','She fell and hurt her knee.','Elle est tombée et s’est blessée au genou.','Knee means…',['genou',’coude',’doigt'],0,'Knee means genou.'),
_u7(47,'Describe pain with hurts','Use hurt or hurts to say that a body part causes pain.','My left foot hurts.','Mon pied gauche me fait mal.','Complete: My head ___.',['hurt',’hurts',’hurting'],1,'Head is singular, so use hurts.'),
_u7(48,'Describe pain with painful','Painful is an adjective meaning causing pain.','The movement is painful.','Le mouvement est douloureux.','Painful means…',['causing pain',’without cost',’very colourful'],0,'Painful describes something that causes pain.'),
_u7(49,'Health advice conversation','Combine should and a reason when giving practical advice.','You should rest because you look exhausted.','Tu devrais te reposer parce que tu sembles épuisé.','Which sentence gives advice and a reason?',['Rest now!','You should rest because you look tired.','You rested yesterday.'],1,'The sentence combines advice with because.'),
_u7(50,'Review: health and feelings','Choose language that describes a symptom and recommends a sensible next step.','I have a fever, so I should speak to a health professional.','J’ai de la fièvre, donc je devrais consulter un professionnel de santé.','Which sentence is grammatically correct?',['I has fever and should to rest.','I have a fever and should rest.','I having fever should resting.'],1,'Use have with I and should + base verb.'),
];
